# ORS then SRS (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (w); Dave 2026-10-19: fix now).
# Leg 1, a sound deck: CassWithExitPupil.in, the exit-pupil Return surface (element 5) and the
#   detector (element 6).  The surface's focal length is first set 2.5% long with MODify; ORS
#   recovers the design value (5.5601, pinned to 5 figures), SRS re-slaves the detector to it, and
#   the OPD at the detector is back at the round-off floor (a bound, pin rule 1).
# Leg 2, a starved deck: ImageDemo.in loses 726 of 741 rays before its exit pupil (surface misses
#   at elements 5-8, finding 1.2 (cc)).  ORS used to print 'TTL OPD= NaN' there and offer a surface
#   optimized on NaN comparisons (the manual's 10-19 morning transcript); the trial rms now counts
#   only rays that reach the surface, an empty trial is a huge merit, and a start with fewer than
#   three data rays is named and aborted -- the must-fail leg: the pre-fix binary prints the NaN.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in
old $TMP/CassWithExitPupil.in
mod
fElt(5)=5.7
q
ors
5
yes
srs
6
5
yes
opd 6
/null
old $TMP/ImageDemo.in
ors
12
# EXPECT: fElt\(\s*5\) =\s+5\.700000000D\+00
# EXPECT: Reference surface optimization results:\s+TTL OPD=\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d\s+nCalls=\s+\d+\s+Old f=\s+5\.700000000D\+00\s+New f=\s+5\.5601\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: Enter number of element to slave to: \[1\]: 5\s+Reference surface recalculation results:
# EXPECT: OPD: nPassRays =\s+112,[\s\S]*RMS OPD error is\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d
# EXPECT: ORS: only\s+\d+ of\s+317 test rays reach element\s+11 \(the surface before it\); at least 3 are needed\.\s+ORS: command aborted\.
# EXPECT-NOT: TTL OPD=\s+NaN
# EXPECT-NOT: New f=\s+\d\.\d+D\+41
# EXPECT-NOT: Debug: VAR_NAM
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
